{"type":"npc","name":"Pollen Brawler","folder":null,"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":120,"temp":0,"max":120,"details":""},"ac":{"value":23,"details":""},"allSaves":{"value":"–2 status to all saves vs. air effects"},"speed":{"value":25,"otherSpeeds":[{"type":"fly","value":10}],"details":"forest passage, lightweight"},"immunities":[{"type":"bleed","exceptions":[]},{"type":"paralyzed","exceptions":[]},{"type":"poison","exceptions":[]},{"type":"sleep","exceptions":[]}]},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":["fey","muan"],"details":""},"level":{"value":6},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>Pollen brawlers are animated elemental spirits composed of millions of individual particles of pollen who help propagate various species of plants within their home regions. Stealthy and cautious, pollen brawlers are known for wrapping themselves around trees or concealing themselves within large bushes, only to erupt without warning when creatures antagonistic to them pass too close to their hiding place.</p><p>When left to their own devices, pollen brawlers wander the land peacefully, exchanging pollen with plants as they go. Druids often call upon pollen brawlers to help defend sacred groves or other significant locations from various threats. Conservationists and disaster recovery specialists also prize pollen brawlers for their ability to help rekindle ecosystems in the aftermath of a natural disaster. However, those who call upon a pollen brawler to rekindle local plants must take care, since pollen brawlers don't distinguish between invasive species and native ones. In fact, when invasive species proliferate at a seemingly impossible rate or foliage quickly overcomes an abandoned street, a pollen brawler might be responsible.</p><p>Pollen brawlers recognize that other creatures consume plants as a part of the natural cycle, and they don't interfere with anyone seeking to harvest plants from their groves. However, they react violently to attempts to eradicate even a single one of the species they propagate, a tendency that can lead to conflict with loggers seeking land development, individuals attempting to reclaim their lands from an invasion of poison oak, or farmers attempting to clear out a new field.</p><h2>Pollen Allergies</h2><p>Some people are severely allergic to pollen—a condition that can be both a detriment and a boon when battling pollen brawlers. Allergic creatures must attempt a Fortitude save against hay fever whenever they start their turn within 30 feet of a pollen brawler. While a tendency to go into a sneezing fit in the presence of a pollen brawler makes it difficult to adequately defend oneself, it's also a counter to the pollen brawler's skill at staying undetected.</p><h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2><p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 30/65/125 gp</p><p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (bludgeoning), armor (light), perception item, skill items (Acrobatics, Athletics, Stealth)</p><p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> bane, constitution, dexterity, energy resistant (vitality), poison, poisonous armor, sensory (darkvision, scent), tangle shield, throwing, wild, winged, wood</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary: Elemental Storm (Pathfinder)","authors":"Mark Adkins","license":"ORC","remaster":true}},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":0.941,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":3},"dex":{"mod":5},"con":{"mod":4},"int":{"mod":-2},"wis":{"mod":1},"cha":{"mod":0}},"perception":{"details":"","mod":11,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision"},{"type":"scent","acuity":"imprecise","range":30}],"vision":true},"saves":{"fortitude":{"value":14,"saveDetail":""},"reflex":{"value":17,"saveDetail":""},"will":{"value":11,"saveDetail":""}},"skills":{"acrobatics":{"base":15,"special":[]},"athletics":{"base":13,"special":[]},"stealth":{"base":13,"special":[{"label":"in vegetation","predicate":[{"or":["terrain:vegetation","terrain:plants"]}],"base":15}]}},"traits":{"value":["elemental","plant"],"rarity":"uncommon","size":{"value":"med"}}},"_id":"iNQzXZxN215iaoQC","img":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/portraits/pollen-brawler.webp","prototypeToken":{"name":"Pollen Brawler","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false,"width":1,"height":1,"texture":{"src":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/tokens/pollen-brawler.webp","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"offsetX":0,"offsetY":0,"fit":"contain","scaleX":2,"scaleY":2,"rotation":0,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"attributes.hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":null},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":[],"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":true,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":2,"texture":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/subjects/pollen-brawler.webp"}},"flags":{"pf2e":{"linkToActorSize":true,"autoscale":false}},"randomImg":false,"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null},"items":[{"img":"systems/pf2e/icons/actions/Passive.webp","name":"–2 Status to All Saves Vs. Air Effects","system":{"actionType":{"value":"passive"},"actions":{"value":null},"category":"defensive","description":{"value":"","gm":""},"publication":{"license":"ORC","remaster":true,"title":"Pathfinder Monster Core","authors":""},"rules":[{"key":"FlatModifier","predicate":["item:trait:air"],"selector":"saving-throw","type":"statu